# Byte-exact checkout on every platform.
#
# The benchmark verifies its own task files by hash — see
# ollama-bench/results/v4-test-hashes.txt, checked with `sha256sum -c` before
# and after a campaign to prove no taker altered a task. Task files were
# authored on Windows and carry CRLF terminators. With git's default
# normalization (core.autocrlf=true here) those bytes would be stored as LF
# and checked out as LF on Linux, so every recorded hash would fail on a
# devbox or WSL clone. Disable conversion entirely rather than re-baselining
# the hashes.
* -text
